{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnumeral\/mode\/harmonicminor"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"harmonicMinor","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Harmonic minor mode, which sharpens the 7th degree.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumeral","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumeral\/Mode"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumeral\/Mode\/harmonicMinor","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"harmonicMinor","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"case","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL10MXLNumeralV4ModeO13harmonicMinoryA2EmF","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Case","title":"MXLNumeral.Mode.harmonicMinor"},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNumeral":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLNumeral","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnumeral","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"MXLNumeral","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumeral","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The numeral type represents the Roman numeral or Nashville number part of a harmony. It requires that the key"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be specified in the encoding, either with a key or numeral-key element."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLNumeral","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNumeral/Mode/harmonicMinor":{"fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"harmonicMinor","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumeral\/Mode\/harmonicMinor","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Harmonic minor mode, which sharpens the 7th degree.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"MXLNumeral.Mode.harmonicMinor","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnumeral\/mode\/harmonicminor"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNumeral/Mode":{"title":"MXLNumeral.Mode","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnumeral\/mode","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The numeral-mode type specifies the mode similar to the mode type, but with a restricted set of values. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"different minor values are used to interpret numeral-root values of 6 and 7 when present in a minor key. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"harmonic minor value sharpens the 7 and the melodic minor value sharpens both 6 and 7. If a minor mode is used"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"without qualification, either in the mode or numeral-mode elements, natural minor is used."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Mode"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Mode"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumeral\/Mode"}}}